Observations:
- Bots advance but very slowly: after 17 game-sec, SUTRA is at dB=6.8 (near site B!) — good progress. But TIGRE is STUCK at (6,19) with target MURALHA repeatedly — it sees an enemy far away (42m, LOS) and fightTarget runs instead of followObjective, strafing in place at spawn area. `think()` finds targets up to 52m with dot > -0.15 — bots snipe across the whole map and stay engaged forever, never advancing. Meanwhile MURALHA (defender) stays at its site. TIGRE strafes at 42m — with sniper-ish accuracy... it fights from 42m.

- SUTRA reaches dB 6.8 but hasn't planted: needs distance < radius−0.35 = 5.05 of site center. It's circling (12,−14)→(8,−8)... goal = site center + holdOffset — holdOffset ±2.5 → goal could be 3-4.6m from center → within radius. dB=6.8 — not yet inside.

- ALSO: botInteract requires `canPlant()` = state ACTIVE. Fine.

The combat-stuck behavior: bots stop objective progress while a distant enemy is visible; fights at 40m across the map. It's realistic-ish but stalls the round. The real issue: `think()` target range 52m is too generous; reduce to ~35m, and if the target is beyond the weapon's effective engagement, still fight. Also the bot strafes forever without closing distance when d > ideal+4 → moveDir adds toTarget — it should close... TIGRE at 42m stuck at (6,19) not moving toward MURALHA — maybe LOS flaky: hasTarget true sometimes (fightTarget strafes velocity ±) but movement damped around 0.

Actually look at TIGRE positions: (5,27) → (6,19) → stays (6,19) for 10+ sec. It probably has target and strafes with perp around... moveDir = toTarget (if d > ideal+4 → move toward target). d = 42 → move toward → but it stays at (6,19)?! Movement blocked? At (6,19) maybe inside a corridor where moveCircle blocks? Position identical (6,19) across 10s — completely stuck. Maybe velocity pushes into a wall and moveCircle blocks both axes; strafe perp also blocked. fightTarget sets velocity toward target + perp; if the bot is against a wall with the target on the other side... then it's pinned. Real bots should fallback: if no movement progress for X sec while in combat → clear target / repath toward objective.

Also: killfeed shows kills (def died) but very slow round progress: after 17s, defenders lost 1. Round will likely time out at 90 with defenders winning 4v3 — bomb never planted. That makes matches boring/one-sided.

Fixes:
1. In `think()`, reduce max engagement range to ~38m and prefer closer targets (already scoring by dist).
2. In `fightTarget`, if distance > ideal+10 and no movement progress → treat as not engaged: clear target, resume objective. Add stuckTimer: track position; if moved < 0.3m over 2.5s while having a target and d > 15 → drop target, set path toward objective.
3. Ensure attackers actually reach inside site: goal currently site.center + holdOffset (±2.5) — that's inside radius 5.4. Once close, plant triggers. But bots stuck fighting prevents arrival. Also `inCombat` check prevents planting while fighting — fine.

Also add: if bot has target but LOS lost > 1.5s → resume objective (already 3s). Reduce to 1.6s.

Also make think() ignore targets when bot is attacker far from objective? Simpler: reduce range to 34m and add stuck handling. Let me implement:

In Bot constructor: this.progressTimer=0; this.lastProgressPos = Vector3.
In update (no-target branch or fightTarget): track progress:
```js
const moved = this.position.distanceTo(this.lastProgressPos);
this.progressTimer += dt;
if (this.progressTimer > 2.2) {
  if (moved < 1.2) {
    // stuck: drop target and force repath
    this.target = null;
    this.destination = null;
    this.repathTimer = 0;
    this.path = [];
  }
  this.lastProgressPos.copy(this.position);
  this.progressTimer = 0;
}
```
Put this in update() after applyMovement. This handles both combat-pinned and path-stuck bots.

Also in think(): `if (dist > 52) continue;` → 36.

And fightTarget closing: keep.

Also — SUTRA at 17s dB=6.8 but site radius 5.4 — goal holds it just outside? holdOffset ±2.5,±2 → max dist from center ~3.2 → inside 5.05. It'll get there if not stuck. The stuck fix will help.

Additionally: defenders vs attackers meeting in middle — kills happen (one def died at ~t 13).

Let me also reconsider `checkElimination` timing — fine.

Implement fixes now.

